In an application under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil 
Procedure, 1908 rule was issued calling upon the opposite parties to 
show cause as to why the impugned judgment and order dated 
07.09.2023 passed by the learned senior District Judge, Dhaka in 
Arbitration Miscellaneous Case No. 330 of 2023 in allowing the 
application appointing the two Arbitrators for both the parties and 
disposed off the same should not be set aside and/or pass such other or 
further order or orders as to this court may seem fit and proper. 
 
I have heard the learned Advocates for the petitioner as well as 
opposite parties. I have perused the impugned judgment and order 
passed by the court below, perused the revisional application, ground 
taken thereon as well as necessary papers and documents annexed 
herewith. 
   Present  
          Mr. Justice Mamnoon Rahman 
 
 
 
 

<<PAGE 2>>
Both the parties agreed that if this court be appointed a sole 
Arbitrator they will accept it and ready to conduct the arbitration in 
question and also they are praying for fixing a time for disposal of the 
matter. 
Considering the facts and circumstances, Mr. Md. Aminul 
Haque, Senior District and Sessions Judge(Retired) and former 
Chairman of 1st Labour Court, Dhaka Address: Flat No. 11-B, New 
Judges Quarter, Azimpur Residential Area, Dhaka (Mobile No. 01711-
200171) be appointed as an Arbitrator to settle the matter with a 
remuneration of Tk. 8,00,000/-(Eight Lac) will be paid by both the 
parties equally and the arbitration tribunal shall conclude the 
proceeding within 4(four) months from the date of receipt of the instant 
order. 
With this observation and direction, the instant rule is disposed 
of. 
Communicate the order at once. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
                (Mamnoon Rahman,J:) 
","PETITIONER is a party to a dispute that was referred to arbitration, and who moved the Senior District Judge at Dhaka in an arbitration miscellaneous case of 2023 for appointment of arbitrators. That court accepted the application and appointed two arbitrators, one for each side. RESPONDENTs are the other parties to the dispute. Both sides agreed before this court that they would accept a sole arbitrator appointed by it and asked for a fixed period for the reference to conclude.","Other: Arbitration Act, 2001",PARTLY,"Since the parties were agreed on the course to be followed, the court did not enter into the merits of the appointment already made below, but substituted its own arrangement for the conduct of the reference. A retired Senior District and Sessions Judge, formerly chairman of a labour court at Dhaka, was appointed sole arbitrator to settle the dispute, with a remuneration of Tk. 8,00,000 to be borne by the parties in equal shares, and the tribunal was directed to conclude the proceeding within four months of receipt of the order. The rule was closed on those terms.",4fe6364ac53be1c0ad990c24dbdc3b5530ea20143788e47c1e0fe09b88955757
