Kabir/BO","PETITIONERs are defendants in a title suit of 2013 at Mohammadpur in Magura over 44 decimals of land, which the Senior Assistant Judge turned down and which the District Judge decreed on appeal in 2017. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs' heirs. The defendants say the appellate court reversed the trial judge without addressing his reasoning, and that the record of rights on which the decree rests does not establish that the plaintiffs held the land exclusively, whether in title or in possession, when the suit was brought.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court examined the three survey records placed on the record, namely the cadastral, the state acquisition and the revisional khatians, and found that the revisional record stood exclusively in the names of the plaintiffs, which supported their claim to exclusive possession. It held that the appellate judge had reasoned the reversal in the manner required of a first appellate court and had not overlooked the trial judge's findings. No merit appearing in the defendants' submission, the rule was brought to an end and the appellate decree left standing.",003b3faa6e45ebc2f8643ffe254689250636a426941b1d7691fb470bceda040d
