","PETITIONERs are defendants in a title suit of 2008 at Shibchar in Madaripur for redemption of a usufructuary mortgage, which the Senior Assistant Judge decreed in part in 2017 and whose appeal was turned down by the District Judge in 2019. RESPONDENT is the plaintiff. The defendants say the plaintiff's kabala of 1997 and the ekranama of the same date amounted to a sale, and that the courts below were wrong to treat the transaction as a mortgage and to find that they had failed to prove repayment.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found that a later instrument cannot convert the character of a registered usufructuary mortgage into one of sale, and that the trial judge had held on a detailed analysis that the defendants had failed to prove by legal evidence either the payment of Tk. 20,000 said to have been made or the due execution of the document relied on. That finding had been endorsed by the appellate court and rested on the material on record. No misreading or non-consideration of evidence being shown, the concurrent findings could not be reopened. The rule was closed.",548f3cdb808e0a1f7984a06295d62503c5f522a5b5b68eca287062c6fdafd00d
