","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a defendant in a suit of 2020 at Kalai in Joypurhat over the suit land, who sought a temporary injunction restraining the plaintiff from interfering with it. The Senior Assistant Judge turned the application down in January 2021 and the District Judge affirmed that later in the year, though this court had meanwhile ordered that the existing position be preserved. RESPONDENT is the plaintiff. The heirs say the refusal left them exposed while the suit itself sat undecided year after year.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"The court observed that the suit had been pending since 2020 without progress, and that a dispute of this kind is better settled once and for all than through interlocutory orders, particularly where the preservation order had held the ring since 2021. Rather than deciding the injunction question itself, it closed the rule with directions: the trial court was to decide the suit on merit by 30 June 2025, without adjournment to either side, and to report the disposal to this court through the Registrar within seven days; the existing preservation order was to continue until then.",6a77a3bb69024661036b86094224515cc24da16877f60ec472abd54cf2c33bb8
