","PETITIONER is a defendant in a suit of 2012 at Raiganj in Sirajganj for a permanent injunction, which the Assistant Judge turned down in 2018 and which the Joint District Judge then decreed on appeal in 2021. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs. The defendant says the plaintiffs' claim rested on an alleged family compromise and on a title they never established, and that a suit for a permanent injunction cannot be used as a way of having a question of title settled in their favour.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that the plaintiffs sought to restrain the defendant from dealing with 4.32 acres without establishing their title to it, and held that a suit framed for a permanent injunction is not the proper vehicle for ascertaining title, since a party asserting a right of ownership must come with a suit for declaration. The appellate judge had reversed the trial judge without weighing the evidence and without meeting his reasoning, so the judgment of reversal could not stand. It was effaced, the trial court's disposal was affirmed, and the suit came to an end.",56ce35bc72e7e7d9579cabe8dd8794a9bf47d909f4e7e95ccd30d134d84ed1d8
