","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a defendant in a title suit of 2006 at Sylhet, which the Joint District Judge decreed in 2014 and whose appeal was turned down by the Additional District Judge in 2019. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs. The heirs say the courts below accepted the plaintiffs' account of a family settlement and of the deeds without noticing material contradictions, and that concurrent findings resting on such a record ought not to bind this court in revision merely because the same material might bear another construction.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court went through the two judgments and found that both had considered the plaintiffs' case and the documents relied on, and that the appellate judge had neither misapplied the law nor overlooked evidence nor decided the appeal without judicial application. Concurrent findings of that quality are not to be reopened in revision merely because another view of the same material may be possible. No case for interference at this stage appearing, the rule was brought to an end, the interim stay was recalled, and the concurrent decree was left standing.",a76738559de075138fb5d1a98823e98b02adc2be3ad43a46d91582a95968bcb2
