","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a defendant in a suit of 2009 at Nachole in Chapainawabganj, which the Assistant Judge turned down in 2011 and which the Joint District Judge then decreed on appeal in 2014, accepting the plaintiffs' title through their predecessor and through certain deeds of exchange. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs' heirs. The petitioners say the appellate court reversed the trial judge without addressing his findings on the documents and on the identity of the land covered by them.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court examined the deeds of exchange executed in favour of the plaintiffs' predecessor and the way the courts below had appreciated them, and found that the appellate judge had reached a conclusion open to him on the material and that no error of law, and no omission to consider evidence, had been shown. A finding of that kind, resting on documents and on the pleadings, does not call for interference in revision merely because the trial judge took the opposite view. The rule raised no question requiring further consideration and was brought to an end, the decree below standing undisturbed.",81221786cfa3243b9b178b01491d0b0853bb6460c50269f0ca0114dda2d47246
