","PETITIONERs are defendants in a title suit of 1997 at Sadar in Noakhali, in which the plaintiffs sought a declaration that two deeds of heba of 1982 in favour of a brother were not binding on them. The suit was decreed by the trial court in 2000 and the Additional District Judge affirmed that on appeal in 2001. RESPONDENTs are the plaintiffs' heirs. The defendants say the appellate court affirmed the decree without independently examining the evidence about the execution of the heba deeds and the delivery of possession.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found that the appellate judge had gone into the evidence on the execution of the heba deeds and on possession, and had reached findings concurrent with those of the trial court which were based on that material. No error of law, no omission to consider evidence and no want of judicial application appeared in the judgment of affirmance. Concurrent findings of that character do not call for interference in revisional jurisdiction. The rule therefore had nothing in it and was brought to an end, the interim stay being recalled.",9b12c55f22157e686121d26fd9bd1348ec6a6cb8f91b051f0c68766a1526f97a
