","PETITIONERs are defendants in a title suit of 2002 at Dhaka, in which the plaintiff sought a declaration of title and the annulment of two registered deeds of heba-bil-ewaz. The Assistant Judge struck out the plaint in 2004 under Order 7 rule 11 of the Code of Civil Procedure, and the Additional District Judge then restored the suit on appeal in 2005. RESPONDENT is the plaintiff. The defendants say the appellate court revived a plaint that was barred by law without looking either at the plaint or at the documents annexed to it.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court examined the plaint and the documents accompanying it and found that the trial judge had committed no error in striking the plaint out, since the relief the plaintiff sought could not be had on the case as pleaded. The appellate judge, on the other hand, had reached the opposite conclusion without considering the plaint itself or the material annexed to it, which was an error of law going to the root of the disposal. The rule was answered in the defendants' favour, the appellate judgment was effaced, and the order of the trial court was restored.",8d0b39912de02f23c2db224dcb1ef0b22e74ad7747c0598ee60cd2b154966730
