","PETITIONER is the son of a lessee who had been allotted a plot of about 280 square yards in Uttara Model Town at Dhaka under a registered lease deed of 1980, and who was convicted in 2022 under section 420 of the Penal Code, 1860 of cheating in connection with the transfer of that plot, and sentenced to seven years with a fine of Tk. 3,00,00,000. RESPONDENTs are the state and the Anti-Corruption Commission. He appeals, saying the transaction was a private sale and no deception was practised on anyone.","Other: Penal Code, 1860",ALLOWED,"The court found that the complaint arose out of the transfer of the plot among the heirs of the original lessee and the person to whom it was later conveyed, and that the person said to have been deceived had never been examined as a witness and had made no allegation that the sellers had taken her money and conveyed the land to another. It held that what was on the record was a pure and simple civil dispute about the sale of land, in which no ingredient of cheating had been established. The conviction and sentence were therefore effaced and the appellant acquitted of the charge.",d457b2c1c0bd08b115b2ebe9372f2c204391b186900fe4ecb4e4582081f2d434
