","PETITIONER is a plaintiff who sued in 2008 at Patharghata in Barguna for partition of a share of 1.99 acres out of a holding of 8.16 acres, whose suit was decreed by the Assistant Judge in 2018 and whose decree was then reversed on appeal in 2023. RESPONDENTs are the defendants. He says the appellate court failed to see that the holding had passed by successive transfers and that a partition was the only remedy that would give each co-sharer his due.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found that the dispute as framed could not be resolved in a partition suit at all, since the plaintiff sought relief against particular defendants on the basis of transactions that required to be avoided in a separate proceeding, and that the courts below had entertained a suit that ought never to have been laid in that form. It held, however, that the plaintiff should not suffer for the way his advocate had drafted the plaint, and that the ends of justice would be met by leaving him free to bring a suit of the proper kind, the time spent in this litigation being excluded when limitation was counted. The rule was brought to an end.",8322972556c6dc2518516243a572d2af6e662459a0dc385652ad74360e49dd69
