","PETITIONER was an upper division assistant in the Water Development Board at Rangpur, convicted in 2023 under sections 26(2) and 27(1) of the Anti-Corruption Commission Act, 2004 on a complaint that she had acquired assets beyond her known sources of income, and sentenced to a year's rigorous imprisonment on the first count and three years with a fine of Tk. 43,00,172 on the second, that sum being confiscated. RESPONDENTs are the state and the Commission. She appeals, saying the inquiry was slipshod and the valuations inflated.","Other: Anti-Corruption Commission Act, 2004",ALLOWED,"The court found that the investigating officer had not excluded the construction cost borne by the appellant's husband, had adduced no evidence about a bank deposit of Tk. 2,89,066 that formed part of the calculation, and had never established the rate of construction for the relevant years, nor measured the area of the building before submitting a fresh report and issuing notice to a young widow. The comparison of assets against income was therefore unsupported at its foundations. The charge was not proved beyond reasonable doubt, and the conviction and sentence were effaced.",d1c7ae2ec9c25367e8f58039a54a0f6da9fcfe9cc7b08106e003ad374ea265eb
