","PETITIONER is a pre-emptee against whom a pre-emption case was brought at Natore, and who obtained a rule in a civil revision in 2016. At the hearing both sides appeared and placed before the court a joint application stating that they had settled the dispute between themselves outside court and had executed a compromise deed in December 2024, which they asked the court to accept. RESPONDENTs are the pre-emptors. The question for the court was whether the settlement could be given effect to in the revision.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"The court examined the terms of the deed executed by the parties and found them to be bona fide and lawful, neither side being under any disability and both being represented by counsel who joined in the application. It accordingly acceded to the joint request and closed the rule in terms of the compromise, directing that the deed form part of the order, recalling the stay that had operated during the revision, and recording that neither side would bear the costs of the proceeding.",b6e0fc1dcde5d35902f564ed30bf9e7121f7322dbfd8807c01684f7bbe7a443c
