","PETITIONER is a plaintiff in a suit of 2023 at Dhaka over family property, whose application under Order 38 rule 5 read with section 151 of the Code to attach the property before judgment was turned down in May 2024. RESPONDENTs are the defendants. She says the first defendant is disposing of the property, that the annexures filed with her supplementary affidavit show he has already done so, and that unless the property is secured the decree she may obtain would be worthless.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"The court found that the material filed with the supplementary affidavit falsified the first defendant's assertion that nothing had been transferred, but observed that the order preserving the position which it had made when the rule was issued had already secured the subject matter, so that neither side stood to be prejudiced while the suit was heard. Rather than decide the attachment application itself, it closed the rule with a direction that the existing order continue until the suit was disposed of, and that the trial court hear and decide the suit within three months.",a70a22c9f62dd89a7fdbf2d3c143cffd67a5ed67c2fbb1ef4848bcb475f70f74
