","PETITIONERs are third parties in a mortgage execution case of 1996 before the Artha Rin Adalat at Chattogram, who objected to the attachment of property in which they claimed an interest, and whose application under Order 21 rule 58 of the Code was dealt with by an order of June 1998 that they say disposed of their claim without any consideration of the material they had placed on record. RESPONDENT is the decree holder bank. They say the executing court never applied its mind to the claim.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that an executing court has a duty to adjudicate finally all questions that arise relating to the execution of the decree, including claims to property attached in execution, and that the court below had failed to apply its judicial mind to the objection raised by the third parties. The order was therefore unsustainable. It was effaced, and the executing court was directed to proceed with the execution and to dispose of the claim application under Order 21 rule 58 on the merits within two months, the case being of considerable age.",6eaa4aa8bf067fc2cdbdcf710eef8a9e1f6acee0bce0db505eb892c115f3b037
