Assistant Bench Officer 
","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a plaintiff who sued in 1996 at Chhagalnaiya in Feni for a declaration of title over 99 decimals and for recovery of possession of part of it, whose suit was turned down by the Senior Assistant Judge in 1997 and whose appeal was turned down by the Joint District Judge in 2001. RESPONDENTs are the defendants. The heirs say the courts below failed to appreciate the old cadastral records, which show their predecessor's share in the holding.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found that both courts below had, on the oral and documentary evidence, concurrently held that the plaintiffs had not proved lawful possession of the land covered by the first schedule of the plaint, nor their earlier possession and subsequent dispossession from the land in the second schedule, and that those findings rested on the evidence. No misreading or non-consideration of evidence being alleged, concurrent findings of that character cannot be reopened in revision. No substance appearing in the petition, the rule was brought to an end.",a9d3e2639cfb87dbac40d35e2140ad520ac4f81023ea4447ae129a7350a8f3d4
