","PETITIONER is a pre-emptee against whom a co-sharer brought a pre-emption case in 2015 at Munshiganj over 5.75 decimals conveyed by a registered kabala of October 2005, and whose appeal against the pre-emption decree was pending when the Joint District Judge, by an order of May 2023, turned down his applications to file an additional written objection and to recall the pre-emptor's first witness for further cross-examination. RESPONDENTs are the pre-emptor and the vendor. He says he was shut out from meeting the case against him.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that the two applications went to the manner in which the pre-emption case had been conducted and that the party against whom the case was decreed ought to have been given a chance to amend his objection, to cross-examine the pre-emptor's witness further and to lead further evidence, so that the appeal could be decided on a full record rather than on an incomplete one. The order turning both applications down was therefore effaced, and the appellate court was directed to allow them and dispose of the appeal on merit within six months.",543702434d09406e432130c334ccaca85497a424e7f091ca04b29e3f40151ae7
