","PETITIONER is a plaintiff whose suit of 2008 at Galachipa in Patuakhali sought a declaration that the judgment and preliminary decree in a partition suit of 2004, and the orders passed in the execution arising from it, were collusive and not binding on him. The Assistant Judge turned the suit down and the Joint District Judge affirmed that in 2016. RESPONDENTs are the heirs of the defendant. He says he was never served with summons in the partition suit and that a minor's interest was affected without the court's leave.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found that both courts below had concurrently held, on the evidence, that summons in the partition suit had been duly served on the plaintiff in his capacity as a defendant there, and that neither his interest nor that of the minor had been affected by the partition decree or by the orders in execution. Those findings rested on the record, and no misreading or non-consideration of evidence was alleged, so that this court could not interfere with them in revision. The rule was brought to an end.",261e9ab3bc7aafdc01836fb419b33a5f5d2c42cc0f8666131b05770f470f892b
