","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a plaintiff who sued in 1996 at Chhagalnaiya in Feni for a declaration of title over six decimals, claiming that his predecessor had taken a settlement of the land from the Maharaja of Tripura by a registered kabuliyat of 1953, and had built shops on it. The Senior Assistant Judge decreed the suit in 1997 and the Joint District Judge effaced that decree on appeal in 2001. RESPONDENTs are the government and others. The heirs say the settlement and long possession were established.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that the plaintiffs' predecessor had obtained the land by a registered deed of kabuliyat executed in 1953, that the cadastral record had been prepared correctly in consequence, and that the manner and mode of the plaintiffs' possession, including the shops standing on the land, showed continuous and peaceful enjoyment over a long period. The trial judge had rightly held title and possession proved and decreed the suit. The appellate judge, though finding the plaintiffs in peaceful possession, had gone on to dismiss the suit, which was a serious illegality. The trial decree was restored.",8326b42aa986d550ec354605955adb2d45dfa4038a6e68f48634d0f498db5526
