","PETITIONERs are plaintiffs whose suit of 2015 at Dhobaura in Mymensingh sought a declaration that a pre-emption order passed in 1993 was unlawful, void and not binding on them. The Assistant Judge struck out the plaint in 2017 under Order 7 rule 11 of the Code of Civil Procedure and the Joint District Judge affirmed that in 2022. RESPONDENT is the defendant. They say the plaint disclosed a triable issue and that the bar of res judicata was a matter for trial rather than for the threshold.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,REFUSED,"The court found that a plain reading of the plaint itself showed that the very issue the plaintiffs sought to raise had already been finally determined by the Appellate Division in the pre-emption proceedings, so that the suit was barred by section 11 of the Code of Civil Procedure on the statements in the plaint alone, which is all that is looked at on such an application. The trial judge had therefore struck the plaint out correctly, and on the plaint rather than on the defendant's submissions. No illegality appearing, the rule was brought to an end.",f32a099bc6c612a266494adcf53c4b074cb5b737e822a14a640877d0dd56ff70
