MD. MASUDUR RAHMAN 
     BENCH OFFICER 
","PETITIONERs are the heirs of a plaintiff who sued in 1997 at Homna in Cumilla for a declaration of title over 31 decimals, tracing the land through a brother said to have inherited it from a widow who died issueless and through his five sons. The Assistant Judge decreed the suit in part in 1999 and the Joint District Judge affirmed that in 2002. RESPONDENTs are the defendants. The heirs say the courts below never required the plaintiffs to prove that the brother was in fact the widow's heir.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,ALLOWED,"The court found that the plaintiffs had failed altogether to prove by legal evidence either that their ancestor was the brother of the widow or that he had inherited the 30 decimals in dispute from her, and that he had been in possession of it, and that both courts below had failed to appreciate that the entire chain of title rested on those two unproved facts. A decree of partition cannot stand on an unproved chain of descent. The decree of the trial court and the affirmance of it were therefore effaced, and the suit came to an end on contest without costs.",91b66fd769c34433a484d088b7a2dd7bd3b1884200ccf782ab822ab7b1b96213
